    "physical_description": "A set of seven shadow puppets made of hide and mounted on wood or bone sticks, and gilded and coloured.\r\n\r\n1. Hanoman, the Monkey General. He has white skin, a long curling tail, gold teeth, and a ferocious face.\r\n\r\n2. Arjuna, the hero. He has golden skin and a black face, wears a gold and coloured garment.\r\n\r\n3. King Suyudana. Similiar in appearance to Arjuna, but he has a golden face and an elaborated head-dress.\r\n\r\n4. A prince (possibly Arjuna), with golden skin and a black face, a black garment and a crown.\r\n\r\n5. A princess. She has a golden skin and a black face, and long black hair.\r\n\r\n6. A princess, with golden skin and a crown, similar to 5.\r\n\r\n7. A demon. He has green skin, gold teeth, and a fierce expression, and is dressed in black, red and gold.",
    "summary": "These puppets are of the traditional type used in the Javanese theatre, and made in the traditional style.",
